{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.6501 accuracy. The strongest evidence shows that learned encoders (scvi_n200) outperform PCA, and avgpool beats transformer for aggregation. The key remaining uncertainty in the RNA-only space is whether scgpt, another learned encoder, can match or exceed scvi_n200 under identical conditions. Config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) isolates exactly this encoder comparison while holding aggregation and profile setting constant. This is the best use of experiment 6 because: (1) it is a clean single-variable comparison that reduces uncertainty about which encoder to build upon, (2) if scgpt is superior, we gain a new best direction to exploit in the remaining 4 experiments (e.g., multimodal scgpt), and (3) if scgpt is inferior, we confirm scvi_n200 as the optimal encoder and can confidently pivot to testing whether multimodal fusion with the best RNA encoder adds value. This avoids the risk of jumping to multimodal (where image alone was very weak at 0.21) before fully characterizing the RNA encoder landscape."
}

